<title>FRANCE: Algeria still negotiating to buy 150,000 T wheat.</title>
<headline>Algeria still negotiating to buy 150,000 T wheat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria is still negotiating the purchase of 150,000 tonnes of wheat, European grain traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;They haven't bought any wheat yet,&quot; one exporter said, adding tender results were expected later on Thursday.</p>
<p>One exporter said Algeria was also discussing the purchase of 40,000 tonnes of U.S. maize for delivery between July 5 and July 15, but others said they were not aware of that tender.</p>
<p>Algeria tendered on Tuesday for 150,000 tonnes of soft wheat for shipment in the second half of August and in September.</p>
<p>Algeria is looking for wheat from the United States, Canada, Argentina, or the European Union, excluding Britain, exporters said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
